{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 128, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling the empty direct input-output edge with a conv adds a strong residual path, while replacing an existing skip/pool brings little or negative gain (exp 1-2 vs 4-7)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the identity shortcut on edge 3 with a conv loses the residual path and hurts accuracy (exp 4-5, inverse of 25)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a shortcut where none existed gives large gains (exp 26) compared with replacing conv/pool ops on edge 3 (exp 25, 27, 28)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 5 absent, edge 3 carries more of the output signal, so upgrading it matters more (exp 2 vs 1, 7 vs 6)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 5 when edge 3 is absent leaves few or no paths to the output, which can collapse accuracy (exp 14, 18 vs 13, 17)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct edge 3, removing edge 0 can disconnect the cell (exp 23, 24 vs 19-22)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Skip-dominated cells are very weak, so swapping a skip for a conv yields large gains (exp 53, 91) compared with replacing a 1x1 conv (exp 65)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing a parameter-free skip on edge 0 costs nothing or even helps (exp 76), whereas removing a conv loses capacity (exp 19-24)."}, {"e